WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.120
(light music)

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.050
- [Narrator] In the
waters around Sri Lanka,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.763
you'll find the world's
only stilt fishermen.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.310
Perched atop a handmade
stilt driven into the sand,

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.323
these fishermen are some
of the last of their kind.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.950
But for those who still fish,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.990
it is about carrying on a tradition

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.093
only found in this part of the world.

00:00:29.684 --> 00:00:32.184
(light music)

00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:37.460
(acoustic guitar music)

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.000
- [Narrator] The history of stilt fishing

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.330
is said to go back to World War II,

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.260
when food shortages and
a lack of proper boats

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.530
caused fishermen to get
creative for their catch.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.973
Fishing from a stick offshore
helped them catch more fish.

00:01:22.197 --> 00:01:24.614
(soft music)

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.880
- [Narrator] Fishing isn't
as lucrative as it once was,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.320
so most stilt fishermen have
other jobs to pay the bills

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.853
but continue to stilt fish
to keep the tradition alive.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.247
(soft music)

00:02:12.293 --> 00:02:16.043
(high-pitched tone resounds)

